    {
      "id": "0bmAt3t3W-KUPyyUPp_TZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 25,
      "y": 1155,
      "width": 460.9072265625,
      "height": 247.5,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b04",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1723275863,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 488283417,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793334668292,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": " First connection, A to B\n 1. A signs in to Clerk and holds T1.\n 2. plxd A asks the relay for the account's hosts (T1): B's hostId.\n 3. A tries B's learned LAN routes. None answer, so it gets a\n    ticket (T1) and opens /connect.\n 4. The relay tells B, and B opens /streams/:id to its :7341.\n 5. TLS 1.3 inside: B's key thumbprint must equal hostId.\n 6. A gets a fresh T2 and posts it with a DPoP proof to\n    /api/auth/account. The relay never sees T2.\n 7. B checks T2 against Clerk's JWKS and sub == its account.\n 8. B issues a DPoP session. Later connections reuse it.",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "steps",
      "originalText": " First connection, A to B\n 1. A signs in to Clerk and holds T1.\n 2. plxd A asks the relay for the account's hosts (T1): B's hostId.\n 3. A tries B's learned LAN routes. None answer, so it gets a\n    ticket (T1) and opens /connect.\n 4. The relay tells B, and B opens /streams/:id to its :7341.\n 5. TLS 1.3 inside: B's key thumbprint must equal hostId.\n 6. A gets a fresh T2 and posts it with a DPoP proof to\n    /api/auth/account. The relay never sees T2.\n 7. B checks T2 against Clerk's JWKS and sub == its account.\n 8. B issues a DPoP session. Later connections reuse it.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "hORoCbbADG_n40GbsVrqF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1095,
      "y": 1155,
      "width": 405.369140625,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b05",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 665827191,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 1295785207,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793334668292,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": " Trust (Ryan's call 1)\n The relay can't: read or change a stream (pinned TLS),\n set B's account (only a trusted local caller does), or\n mint a session with a key of its own.\n The relay can: drop or delay streams, see who is online,\n and if compromised, list a fake host of its own, catch\n the T2 a client sends it, and use it on the real hosts\n within about 6 minutes.\n Accepted as T3 accepts its relay. A client that must not\n trust the relay pairs with a code instead (0065).",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "trust",
      "originalText": " Trust (Ryan's call 1)\n The relay can't: read or change a stream (pinned TLS),\n set B's account (only a trusted local caller does), or\n mint a session with a key of its own.\n The relay can: drop or delay streams, see who is online,\n and if compromised, list a fake host of its own, catch\n the T2 a client sends it, and use it on the real hosts\n within about 6 minutes.\n Accepted as T3 accepts its relay. A client that must not\n trust the relay pairs with a code instead (0065).",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
